# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI-Team — What Does NOT Belong in the Framework Repository
#
# This repository holds the framework only: roles, procedures, diagrams, and
# templates. Everything specific to an individual project is created during
# bootstrap (Procedure P-0) and lives in the project repository. Anyone who
# clones this framework must receive a clean, empty frame with zero foreign
# project tasks or measurements.
#
# Simple rule: if a file contains a project name, a measurement number from a
# project run, a task, or someone else's name — it is project-specific and
# never gets committed here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Task board: plans, findings, questions, and completed work log.
# Templates live in templates/board/ and are versioned; the live board is not.
/board/

# Role memory: what a role knows about THIS project, its craft, and decisions.
# Templates live in templates/memory/; populated memory is project-specific.
/memory/

# Project passport: gates, content rules, territories, generators, and testbed.
# Populated from templates/PROJECT.md.
/PROJECT.md
/PROJECT-*.md

# Session and run reports / handoffs.
/reports/
/*-report.md
/*-handoff.md
/STATE.md

# Project-specific sources (internal links and standards).
/SOURCES-PROJECT.md

# Frames, logs, snapshots, scratch files.
/shots/
/logs/
*.log
/.scratch/
/tmp/

# Local IDE and OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Editor lock files (LibreOffice, etc.)
.~lock.*#
*.swp
*~

# Cross-session chat: messages are PROJECT-SPECIFIC and live outside the repo
# (see CROSS-TOOL-CHAT.md §1). Guarded here in case a channel is created locally.
/_chat/
/chat/general/
/chat/roster/
/chat/*/

# Other project-specific directories created during deployment
/prompts/
/diagnostics/
/qa/
/realization-plan/
